    "effect_size": "AE rate: Dimebon 64.6% vs Placebo 64.6% (Cohort 1); Dimebon 55.1% vs Placebo 53.3% (Cohort 2)",
    "p_value": null,
    "target_engagement_evidence": null,
    "biomarker_changes": [
      "Urine blood (>=1): Dimebon Cohort 1 32% vs Placebo 7%; Dimebon Cohort 2 26% vs Placebo 5%",
      "Magnesium (>1.1*ULN): Dimebon Cohort 1 20% vs Placebo 24%; Dimebon Cohort 2 18% vs Placebo 17%",
      "Glucose (>1.5*ULN): Dimebon Cohort 1 9% vs Placebo 10%; Dimebon Cohort 2 6% vs Placebo 4%"
    ],
    "subgroup_findings": [
      "Urine blood abnormality notably higher in Dimebon arms vs placebo in both cohorts (Cohort 1: 32% vs 7%; Cohort 2: 26% vs 5%)",
      "QTcF 450 to <480 msec: Dimebon Cohort 1 15.7% vs Placebo 13.4%; Dimebon Cohort 2 15.6% vs Placebo 19.3%",
      "QTcF >=500 msec: Dimebon Cohort 2 1.2% vs Placebo 0.0%",
      "Decrease in systolic BP >=30 mmHg: Dimebon Cohort 1 16.7% vs Placebo 12.9%"
    ],
    "safety_signals": [
      "Overall AE rates similar between Dimebon and placebo in both cohorts",
      "Urine blood abnormality markedly higher in Dimebon-treated patients vs placebo in both cohorts",
      "Serious adverse events included pancytopenia and thrombotic thrombocytopenic purpura in Dimebon arm",
      "Cardiac serious AEs (AV block complete, bradycardia, congestive cardiac failure, myocardial infarction, sick sinus syndrome) observed predominantly in placebo arm except sick sinus syndrome (1 Dimebon)",
      "QTcF prolongation signals were low and generally comparable between arms"
    ],
